{"raw": {"https://felician.edu/about-felician-university/careers-at-felician/": {"title": "Careers at Felician", "description": "Careers at Felician - Felician University of New Jersey GDPR Cookie Banner Felician University uses cookies to provide necessary website functionality, improve your experience and analyze our traffic. By using our website, you agree to our Privacy Policy and our cookies usage. Accept Skip Navigation MENU MENU News Events My Felician Alumni Giving Menu \u00d7 search About About Felician University The University operates on two campuses in Lodi and Rutherford, New Jersey. The University is one of the institutions of higher learning conducted by the Felician Sisters in the United States. Founded by the Felician Sisters of Lodi, New Jersey, it began as Immaculate Conception Normal School with the first summer session commencing on July 5, 1923. History & Tradition Institutional Research Office of the President Senior Administrative Officers Board of Trustees Members Fast Facts Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Facilities and Resources Faculty and Staff Directory On Campus Tours Virtual Tour Directions & Maps Academics Academics at Felician University Felician University has four schools and an institute for you to explore a range of undergraduate, pre-professional, certificate, and graduate programs. Search through the program offerings and find the program that is right for you in the School of Arts and Sciences, School of Business and Information Sciences, Education, Nursing, or the Institute for Information Sciences. School of Arts & Sciences School of Education School of Business and Information Sciences School of Nursing The Felician Advantage Lenke Family Center for Innovation Center for Career & Academic Success Center for Academic Technology Honors Program Office of the Registrar Catalogs Institutional Review Board Summer Programs Academic Events Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid at Felician University Inspiring courses that make you think, dedicated faculty who will push you further than you imagined, and hands-on experiences that will shape your career and future. No SAT/ACT Required Affordability Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Adult Undergraduate Admissions Transfer Admissions Our Admissions Representatives High School Guidance Counselor Portal Accepted Students International Students Veterans Services Student Financial Services Make Application Payment Parents Virtual and On Campus Tours Become a Corporate Partner Virtual Appointments Admission Events Campus Life Campus Life at Felician University Our goal is to provide our students with a quality out of class experience that supports and amplifies the teaching and learning process which is the heart of our University. Students may choose from a wide range of opportunities which are designed to help them develop their leadership abilities and to have an enjoyable collegiate experience with great memories that will never end. Office of Student Affairs Dining Services Student Handbook Technology Services Students with Disabilities Residence Life The Center for Student Development and Engagement Campus Safety Counseling and Wellness Services Title IX Campus Ministry University Library University Bookstore Emergency Telephone Numbers Parents Bus & Shuttle Schedules Athletics GET INFO VISIT APPLY News Events My Felician Alumni Giving About About Felician University The University operates on two campuses in Lodi and Rutherford, New Jersey. The University is one of the institutions of higher learning conducted by the Felician Sisters in the United States. Founded by the Felician Sisters of Lodi, New Jersey, it began as Immaculate Conception Normal School with the first summer session commencing on July 5, 1923. History & Tradition Institutional Research Office of the President Senior Administrative Officers Board of Trustees Members Fast Facts Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Facilities and Resources Faculty 