on Sciences School of Nursing The Felician Advantage Lenke Family Center for Innovation Center for Career & Academic Success Center for Academic Technology Honors Program Office of the Registrar Catalogs Institutional Review Board Summer Programs Academic Events Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid at Felician University Inspiring courses that make you think, dedicated faculty who will push you further than you imagined, and hands-on experiences that will shape your career and future. No SAT/ACT Required Affordability Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Adult Undergraduate Admissions Transfer Admissions Our Admissions Representatives High School Guidance Counselor Portal Accepted Students International Students Veterans Services Student Financial Services Make Application Payment Parents Virtual and On Campus Tours Become a Corporate Partner Virtual Appointments Admission Events Campus Life Campus Life at Felician University Our goal is to provide our students with a quality out of class experience that supports and amplifies the teaching and learning process which is the heart of our University. Students may choose from a wide range of opportunities which are designed to help them develop their leadership abilities and to have an enjoyable collegiate experience with great memories that will never end. Office of Student Affairs Dining Services Student Handbook Technology Services Students with Disabilities Residence Life The Center for Student Development and Engagement Campus Safety Counseling and Wellness Services Title IX Campus Ministry University Library University Bookstore Emergency Telephone Numbers Parents Bus & Shuttle Schedules Athletics GET INFO VISIT APPLY Home \\ About Felician University \\ Careers at Felician Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services IN THIS SECTION Felician University, the Franciscan University of New Jersey is seeking dynamic, enthusiastic and highly organized full-time professional Administrative Assistant to provide support to the Dean. The Administrative Specialist for Student Success & Accessibility Services is a full-time, in-person, 12-month position with two co-equal areas of responsibility. The role provides direct administrative and operational support to the Dean of Student Success, Retention, & Assessment, including coordination of the Dean\u2019s schedule, communications, meetings, records, reporting, purchasing, events, and assigned priorities. \u00a0The role also supports the Office of Accessibility Services, providing administrative and logistical support for approved accommodations, testing coordination, student and faculty communications, confidential records, and related service workflows in partnership with the Coordinator of Accessibility Services. The position serves as a primary point of contact for the Dean\u2019s office and accessibility services and requires exceptional organization, attention to detail, sound judgment, discretion in handling confidential information, and a commitment to responsive, student-centered service and the University mission. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity , Compassion , Transformation , Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. Required Education: Associate degree and a minimum of three years of progressively responsible administrative experience required, BA/BS preferred Qualifications: Relevant experience in higher education, student services, accessibility services, or a similar service environment is preferred; demonstrated reliability, initiative, sound judgment, attention to detail, and commitment to responsive, student-centered service; demonstrated ability to adapt to changing priorities, procedures, technologies, and service needs while managing competing responsibilities effectively; demonstrated ability to collaborate and communicate effectively, professionally, and with appropriate discretion when serving students, faculty, staff, families, and campus partners; demonstrated ability to handle confidential student information with discretion and to maintain accurate, secure records in accordance with University policies and established procedures; demonstrated organizational skills and ability to manage multiple calendars, deadlines, records, service requests, and competing priorities accurately across two functional assignments; proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, including Excel, Word, and Outlook, and the ability to use University information systems; accessibility-related platforms, and web-based tools to manage scheduling, communications, records, reporting, and service workflows;\u00a0 willingness and ability to master new computer programs, including student support, accessibility-related, and administrative systems; willingness and ability to support and promote the Felician Franciscan mission and core values of the University. To Apply: Send cover letter, current curriculum vitae, and the names and contact information for (two) 2 professional references electronically to: Dean via USPS to: Dr. Jeffrey Blanchard, Dean, Center for Academic Success & Effectiveness Felician University 1 Felician Way Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 About Felician University CONTACT INFORMATION Felician University One Felician Way Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 Phone: 201.559.6000 Phone: 201.355.1465 Contact Us | Directions & Maps | Campus Emergency Information | Request Information | Students Right to Know and Achievement | Privacy policy | Anti-Discrimination Policy | Accessibility TOP Felician University - One Felician Way, Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 201.559.6000 / 201.355.1465 GDPR Cookie Banner Felician University uses cookies to provide necessary website functionality, improve your experience and analyze our traffic. By using our website, you agree to our Privacy Policy and our cookies usage. Accept Close GDPR Cookie Settings Privacy O