ents Virtual and On Campus Tours Become a Corporate Partner Virtual Appointments Admission Events Campus Life Campus Life at Felician University Our goal is to provide our students with a quality out of class experience that supports and amplifies the teaching and learning process which is the heart of our University. Students may choose from a wide range of opportunities which are designed to help them develop their leadership abilities and to have an enjoyable collegiate experience with great memories that will never end. Office of Student Affairs Dining Services Student Handbook Technology Services Students with Disabilities Residence Life The Center for Student Development and Engagement Campus Safety Counseling and Wellness Services Title IX Campus Ministry University Library University Bookstore Emergency Telephone Numbers Parents Bus & Shuttle Schedules Athletics GET INFO VISIT APPLY Home \\ About Felician University \\ Careers at Felician Faculty Adjunct, Communications IN THIS SECTION Felician University is offering exciting opportunities for Adjunct Faculty in the Communications division of the School of Arts and Sciences for the 2026-2027 academic year. Under the mentorship of full-time faculty, adjunct faculty provide classroom experiences grounded in \u201cbest practices\u201d for higher education and their respective disciplines. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity , Compassion , Transformation , Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. Position Type: Part-time, 1-2 courses per semester, maximum 3 days per week. Day and evening classes, online and traditional formats available. Department: School of Arts & Sciences, Communications Division Required Education: Master\u2019s degree in Communications, Journalism, Media Studies or a related field of expertise requird, Doctoral degree preferred Qualifications: 1+ years\u2019 teaching teaching experience at the baccalaureate level Proven experience of online teaching experence. Demonstrated familiarity with online teching platforms. Ability to engage effectively with a diverse student population. Willingness and ability to support and promote the Felician Franciscan core values and mission of the University To Apply: Send cover letter, current curriculum vitae, and the names and contact information for two professional references electronically to the Associate Dean of Humanities or via USPS to: Dr. Lavina Sequeira, Associate Dean of Humanities School of Arts & Sciences Felician University 262 South Main Street Lodi, New Jersey 07644 Salary: $700-800 per course credit About Felician University CONTACT INFORMATION Felician University One Felician Way Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 Phone: 201.559.6000 Phone: 201.355.1465 Contact Us | Directions & Maps | Campus Emergency Information | Request Information | Students Right to Know and Achievement | Privacy policy | Anti-Discrimination Policy | Accessibility TOP Felician University - One Felician Way, Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 201.559.6000 / 201.355.1465 Close GDPR Cookie Settings Privacy Overview Strictly Necessary Cookies Powered by GDPR Cookie Compliance (opens in a new tab) Privacy Overview This website uses cookies so that we can provide you with the best user experience possible. Cookie information is stored in your browser and performs functions such as recognising you when you return to our website and helping our team to understand which sections of the website you find most interesting and useful. Strictly Necessary Cookies Strictly Necessary Cookie should be enabled at all times so that we can save your preferences for cookie settings. Enabled Disabled Enable All Save Settings Notifications"}, "https://felician.edu/about-felician-university/careers-at-felician/adjmath/": {"title": "Faculty Adjunct", "description": "Faculty Adjunct - Mathematics - Felician University of New Jersey GDPR Cookie Ban