through the program offerings and find the program that is right for you in the School of Arts and Sciences, School of Business and Information Sciences, Education, Nursing, or the Institute for Information Sciences. School of Arts & Sciences School of Education School of Business and Information Sciences School of Nursing The Felician Advantage Lenke Family Center for Innovation Center for Career & Academic Success Center for Academic Technology Honors Program Office of the Registrar Catalogs Institutional Review Board Summer Programs Academic Events Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid at Felician University Inspiring courses that make you think, dedicated faculty who will push you further than you imagined, and hands-on experiences that will shape your career and future. No SAT/ACT Required Affordability Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Adult Undergraduate Admissions Transfer Admissions Our Admissions Representatives High School Guidance Counselor Portal Accepted Students International Students Veterans Services Student Financial Services Make Application Payment Parents Virtual and On Campus Tours Become a Corporate Partner Virtual Appointments Admission Events Campus Life Campus Life at Felician University Our goal is to provide our students with a quality out of class experience that supports and amplifies the teaching and learning process which is the heart of our University. Students may choose from a wide range of opportunities which are designed to help them develop their leadership abilities and to have an enjoyable collegiate experience with great memories that will never end. Office of Student Affairs Dining Services Student Handbook Technology Services Students with Disabilities Residence Life The Center for Student Development and Engagement Campus Safety Counseling and Wellness Services Title IX Campus Ministry University Library University Bookstore Emergency Telephone Numbers Parents Bus & Shuttle Schedules Athletics GET INFO VISIT APPLY Home \\ About Felician University \\ Careers at Felician Assistant Professor, Prelicensure Nursing IN THIS SECTION Felician University is currently seeking experienced, dedicated and academically qualified nursing specialists to teach in the Prelicensure Program of the School of Nursing.\u00a0 Candidates should have experience teaching in both traditional and online venues and must be willing to successfully complete Felician online certification.\u00a0 S/he must have an educational background in the fundamentals of the discipline, as well as a wealth of real-world experience to bring to class discussions and case analyses. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity , Compassion , Transformation , Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. We offer a\u00a0choice of medical, dental, vision, and life insurance benefits, as well as a retirement plan (403B), tuition remission, and generous time off benefits. Required Education: Masters of Science in Nursing required, doctoral degree preferred.\u00a0 Faculty teaching in the graduate program must have an earned doctoral degree or currently enrolled in doctoral program Qualifications: Licensure in New Jersey as a Registered Nurse.\u00a0 Graduate Faculty must have current national certification and NJ Board of Nursing licensure as a Family Nurse Practitioner. 2+ years\u2019 practical experience in the area of specialization. Comprehensive knowledge of and experience in clinical nursing education. Previous teaching experience, preferably in an institution of higher education. Superior written and verbal communications skills. Ability to engage with students of diverse\u00a0backgrounds and experiences. Willingness and ability to support and promote the Felician Franciscan mission and values of the University. To Apply: Send CV and three (3) professional references to Interim Dean or via USPS to: Dr. Patricia Munno, Interim Dean School of Nursing Felician University 262 South Main Street Lodi, New Jersey 07644 Salary Range: $83,000 \u2013 $88,100, commensurate with rank, experience and certifications Contact Information Office of Admissions Rutherford Campus One Felician Way Rutherford, NJ 07070-1612 Phone: 201.355.1465 Fax: 201.355.1443 Office of The Registrar Lodi Campus 262 South Main Street Lodi, NJ 07644 Phone: 201.559.6043 Fax: 201.559.6066 Email: registrar@felician.edu Contact Us | Directions & Maps | Campus Emergency Information | Request Information | Students Right to Know and Achievement | Privacy policy | Anti-Discrimination Policy | Accessibility TOP Felician University - One Felician Way, Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 201.559.6000 / 201.355.1465 GDPR Cookie Banner Felician University uses cookies to provide necessary website functionality, improve your experience and analyze our traffic. By using our website, you agree to our Privacy Policy and our cookies usage. Accept Close GDPR Cookie Settings Privacy Overview Strictly Necessary Cookies Powered by GDPR Cookie Compliance (opens in a new tab) Privacy Overview This website uses cookies so that we can provide you with the best user experience possible. Cookie information is stored in your browser and performs functions such as recognising you when you return to our website and helping our team to understand which sections of the website you find most interesting and useful. Strictly Necessary Cookies Strictly Necessary Cookie should be enabled at all times so that we can save your preferences for cookie settings. Enabled Disabled Enable All Save Settings"}, "https://felician.edu/about-felician-university/careers-at-felician/math/": {"title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Mathematics", "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Mathematics - Felician University of New Jersey Skip Navigation MENU MENU News Events My Felician Alumni Giving Menu About About Felician University The University operates on two campuses in Lodi and Rutherford, New Jersey. The University is one of the institutions of higher learning conducted by the Felician Sisters in the United States. Founded by the Felician Sisters of Lodi, New Jersey, it began as Immaculate Conception Normal School with the first summer session commencing on July 5, 1923. History & Tradition Institutional Research Office of the President Senior Administrative Officers Board of Trustees Members Fast Facts Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Facilities and Resources Faculty and Staff Directory On Campus Tours Virtual Tour Directions & Maps Academics Academics at Felician University Felician University has four schools and an institute for you to explore a range of undergraduate, pre-professional, certificate, and graduate programs. Search through the program offerings and find the program that is right for you in the School of Arts and Sciences, School of Business and Information Sciences, Education, Nursing, or the Institute for Information Sciences. School of Arts & Sciences School of Education School of Business and Information Sciences School of Nursing The Felician Advantage Lenke Family Center for Innovation Center for Career & Academic Success Center for Academic Technology Honors Program Office of the Registrar Catalogs Institutional Review Board Summer Programs Academic Events Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid at Felician University Inspiring courses that make you think, dedicated faculty who will push you further than you imagined, and hands-on experiences that will shape your career and future. No SAT/ACT Required Affordability Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Adult Undergraduate Admissions Transfer Admissions Our Admissions Representatives High School Guidance Counselor Portal Accepted Students International Students Veterans Services Student Financial Services Make Application Payment Parents Virtual and On Campus Tours Become a Corporate Partner Virtual Appointments Admission Events Campus Lif