Sciences School of Nursing The Felician Advantage Lenke Family Center for Innovation Center for Career & Academic Success Center for Academic Technology Honors Program Office of the Registrar Catalogs Institutional Review Board Summer Programs Academic Events Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid at Felician University Inspiring courses that make you think, dedicated faculty who will push you further than you imagined, and hands-on experiences that will shape your career and future. No SAT/ACT Required Affordability Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Adult Undergraduate Admissions Transfer Admissions Our Admissions Representatives High School Guidance Counselor Portal Accepted Students International Students Veterans Services Student Financial Services Make Application Payment Parents Virtual and On Campus Tours Become a Corporate Partner Virtual Appointments Admission Events Campus Life Campus Life at Felician University Our goal is to provide our students with a quality out of class experience that supports and amplifies the teaching and learning process which is the heart of our University. Students may choose from a wide range of opportunities which are designed to help them develop their leadership abilities and to have an enjoyable collegiate experience with great memories that will never end. Office of Student Affairs Dining Services Student Handbook Technology Services Students with Disabilities Residence Life The Center for Student Development and Engagement Campus Safety Counseling and Wellness Services Title IX Campus Ministry University Library University Bookstore Emergency Telephone Numbers Parents Bus & Shuttle Schedules Athletics GET INFO VISIT APPLY Home \\ About Felician University \\ Careers at Felician Assistant/Associate Professor, Mathematics IN THIS SECTION Felician University, the Franciscan University of New Jersey, seeks an academically qualified specialist to serve as Assistant/Associate Professor of Mathematics in the School of Arts and Sciences for the 2025-2026 academic year. Candidates should have experience teaching in a traditional and online environment and must be willing to pursue Felician online certification.\u00a0 S/he must possess comprehensive mathematical expertise to teach across the complete spectrum of undergraduate mathematics courses, from developmental and foundational courses through advanced upper-level offerings required for the bachelor\u2019s degree in mathematics. S/he will serve students at all levels of mathematical preparation utilizing exceptional communication skills to make complex mathematical concepts accessible and engaging for diverse learners. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity , Compassion , Transformation , Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. We offer a\u00a0 choice of medical, dental, vision, and life insurance benefits, as well as a retirement plan (403B), tuition remission, and generous time off benefits. Position Type: Full-time, 10-months, Exempt Department: Mathematics, School of Arts and Sciences Required Education: Earned doctoral degree in Mathematics or related field such as Mathematics Education or Applied Mathematics Qualifications: Demonstrated expertise across the full spectrum of undergraduate mathematics curriculum from developmental through advanced coursework. Minimum of two years teaching experience in mathematics at the college level. Strong verbal and written communication skills with proven ability to explain complex mathematical concepts clearly and effectively. Demonstrated skill in working with students of diverse academic backgrounds and learning styles. Proficiency with mathematical software, learning management systems, and educational technology tools. Ability to adapt teaching methods to accommodate different learning preferences and academic preparation levels. Strong organizational and time management skills. Commitment to fostering an inclusive and supportive learning environment for all students. Ability and willingness to support and promote the Felician Franciscan core values and mission of the University. To Apply: Send cover letter, current curriculum vitae, and the names and contact information for two professional references electronically to the Associate Dean or via USPS to: Dr. Gaby Fahmy, Associate Dean School of Arts and Sciences Felician University 262 South Main Street Lodi, New Jersey 07644 Contact Information Office of Admissions Rutherford Campus One Felician Way Rutherford, NJ 07070-1612 Phone: 201.355.1465 Fax: 201.355.1443 Office of The Registrar Lodi Campus 262 South Main Street Lodi, NJ 07644 Phone: 201.559.6043 Fax: 201.559.6066 Email: registrar@felician.edu Contact Us | Directions & Maps | Campus Emergency Information | Request Information | Students Right to Know and Achievement | Privacy policy | Anti-Discrimination Policy | Accessibility TOP Felician University - One Felician Way, Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 201.559.6000 / 201.355.1465 GDPR Cookie Banner Felician University uses cookies to provide necessary website functionality, improve your experience and analyze our traffic. By using our website, you agree to our Privacy Policy and our cookies usage. Accept Close GDPR Cookie Settings Privacy Overview Strictly Necessary Cookies Powered by GDPR Cookie Compliance (opens in a new tab) Privacy Overview This website uses cookies so that we can provide you with the best user experience possible. Cookie information is stored in your browser and performs functions such as recognising you when you return to our website and helping our team to understand which sections of the website you find most interesting and useful. Strictly Necessary Cookies Strictly Necessary Cookie should be enabled at all times so that we can save your preferences for cookie settings. Enabled Disabled Enable All Save Settings"}, "https://felician.edu/about-felician