 for Student Development and Engagement Campus Safety Counseling and Wellness Services Title IX Campus Ministry University Library University Bookstore Emergency Telephone Numbers Parents Bus & Shuttle Schedules Athletics GET INFO VISIT APPLY Home \\ About Felician University \\ Careers at Felician Academic Success Coach IN THIS SECTION Felician University, the Franciscan University of New Jersey seeking a Nursing professional to serve as a Nursing Success Coach for the upcoming Fall semester.\u00a0 The Nursing Success Coach is responsible for developing and conducting retention and support activities for students identified as \u201cat-risk of failing\u201d in the Hybrid ABSN Nursing Program.\u00a0 S/he provides direct academic support, mentoring and coordinated service delivery plan and connects students to needed resources with the primary purpose of improving course completion and graduation outcomes in the Hybrid ABSN Program. The positions are primarily remote and will require access to and familiarity with remote learning venues, i.e., Zoom, Microsoft teams. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity , Compassion , Transformation , Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. Position Type: Per diem, 12-month, Non-Exempt Department: School of Nursing Date Posted: Monday, August 21, 2023 Required Education: Bachelor\u2019s degree from an accredited institution required, Master\u2019s degree in Nursing preferred. Qualifications: Current NJ license in good standing as a Registered Nurse, NJ Registered Nurse license required throughout employment in the position; knowledge of student development and resources to promote student success; previous experience mentoring or precepting; demonstrated experience maintaining confidentiality (HIPPA and FERPA); strong working knowledge of Microsoft Office applications and online learning platforms such as Canvas LMS; ability, willingness and equipment required to utilize remote instructional venues, i.e., Zoom; strong organizational skills with the ability to work independently; availability and willingness to work a flexible schedule which includes evenings and weekends; ability to effectively track student participation and success rates; ability to communicate effectively with prospective and current students, staff faculty, administration, colleagues and community partners in large and small group settings; ability and willingness to support and promote the Felician Franciscan mission and core values of the University. To Apply: Send cover letter, resume, and the names and contact information for (two) 2 professional references electronically to the Associate Dean or via USPS to: Ms. Jennifer Kostic, Associate Dean for the School of Nursing Felician University 262 South Main Street Lodi, New Jersey 07644 Salary: Commensurate with experience. About Felician University CONTACT INFORMATION Felician University One Felician Way Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 Phone: 201.559.6000 Phone: 201.355.1465 Contact Us | Directions & Maps | Campus Emergency Information | Request Information | Students Right to Know and Achievement | Privacy policy | Anti-Discrimination Policy | Accessibility TOP Felician University - One Felician Way, Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 201.559.6000 / 201.355.1465 Close GDPR Cookie Settings Privacy Overview Strictly Necessary Cookies Powered by GDPR Cookie Compliance (opens in a new tab) Privacy Overview This website uses cookies so that we can provide you with the best user experience possible. Cookie information is stored in your browser and performs functions such as recognising you when you return to our website and helping our team to understand which sections of the website you find most interesting and useful. Strictly Necessary Cookies Strictly Necessary Cookie should be enabled at all times so that we can save your preferences for cookie settings. Enabled 