memories that will never end. Office of Student Affairs Dining Services Student Handbook Technology Services Students with Disabilities Residence Life The Center for Student Development and Engagement Campus Safety Counseling and Wellness Services Title IX Campus Ministry University Library University Bookstore Emergency Telephone Numbers Parents Bus & Shuttle Schedules Athletics GET INFO VISIT APPLY Home \\ About Felician University \\ Careers at Felician Faculty Adjuncts, School of Business and Information Sciences Felician University is offering a variety of exciting opportunities for passionate and experienced educators to join our growing team of Adjunct Faculty in the School of Business and Information Sciences for the 2024-2025 academic year. Our faculty adjuncts help to shape the minds of tomorrow\u2019s leaders and support and promote the next generation of tech-savvy professionals through mentoring students in dynamic Master\u2019s-level courses grounded in real-world applications, delivering engaging instructions using best practices in higher education and areas of expertise, and collaborating with our dedicated full-time faculty to foster a supportive learning environment. Opportunities are available in three areas of academic studies: Computer Science Data Science Cyber Security We offer flexible opportunities to fit your schedule: Part-time positions teaching 1-2 courses per semester. Schedule variety, with daytime, evening, and online courses available to accommodate your preferences. A maximum of 3 days per week to ensure work-life balance. Essential Qualifications include: Master\u2019s degree in Computer Science, Data Science, Cyber Security or a closely related field. Teaching experience, preferably at the graduate level. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to engage with a diverse student population. Passion for sharing knowledge. Demonstrated commitment to student success. Experience with BrightSpace LMS preferred. Ability and willingness to support and promote the Franciscan Felician core values and mission of the University. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity , Compassion , Transformation , Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. To apply, send your cover letter, current CV, and two (2) professional references electronically to S chool of Business and Information Sciences , or via USPS to: Dr. David Turi, Associate Dean School of Business and Information Sciences Felician University 1 Felician Way Rutherford, New Jersey \u00a007070 About Felician University CONTACT INFORMATION Felician University One Felician Way Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 Phone: 201.559.6000 Phone: 201.355.1465 Contact Us | Directions & Maps | Campus Emergency Information | Request Information | Students Right to Know and Achievement | Privacy policy | Anti-Discrimination Policy | Accessibility TOP Felician University - One Felician Way, Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 201.559.6000 / 201.355.1465 Close GDPR Cookie Settings Privacy Overview Strictly Necessary Cookies Powered by GDPR Cookie Compliance (opens in a new tab) Privacy Overview This website uses cookies so that we can provide you with the best user experience possible. Cookie information is stored in your browser and performs functions such as recognising you when you return to our website and helping our team to understand which sections of the website you find most interesting and useful. Strictly Necessary Cookies Strictly Necessary Cookie should be enabled at all times so that we can save your preferences for cookie settings. Enabled Disabled Enable All Save Settings Notifications"}, "https://felician.edu/about-felician-university/careers-at-felician/menswrs/": {"title": "Part-time Assistant Coach, Men\u2019s Wrestling", "description": "Part-time Assistant Coach, Men's Wrestling - Felician University of New Jersey Skip Navigation MENU 