e Institute for Information Sciences. School of Arts & Sciences School of Education School of Business and Information Sciences School of Nursing The Felician Advantage Lenke Family Center for Innovation Center for Career & Academic Success Center for Academic Technology Honors Program Office of the Registrar Catalogs Institutional Review Board Summer Programs Academic Events Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid at Felician University Inspiring courses that make you think, dedicated faculty who will push you further than you imagined, and hands-on experiences that will shape your career and future. No SAT/ACT Required Affordability Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Adult Undergraduate Admissions Transfer Admissions Our Admissions Representatives High School Guidance Counselor Portal Accepted Students International Students Veterans Services Student Financial Services Make Application Payment Parents Virtual and On Campus Tours Become a Corporate Partner Virtual Appointments Admission Events Campus Life Campus Life at Felician University Our goal is to provide our students with a quality out of class experience that supports and amplifies the teaching and learning process which is the heart of our University. Students may choose from a wide range of opportunities which are designed to help them develop their leadership abilities and to have an enjoyable collegiate experience with great memories that will never end. Office of Student Affairs Dining Services Student Handbook Technology Services Students with Disabilities Residence Life The Center for Student Development and Engagement Campus Safety Counseling and Wellness Services Title IX Campus Ministry University Library University Bookstore Emergency Telephone Numbers Parents Bus & Shuttle Schedules Athletics GET INFO VISIT APPLY Home \\ About Felician University \\ Careers at Felician Part-time Assistant Coach, Men\u2019s Wrestling IN THIS SECTION Felician University is currently offering an exciting opportunity for a dynamic, energic, enthusiastic and experienced athletics professional to serve as Assistant Coach for Men\u2019s Wrestling.\u00a0 The Assistant Coach is responsible for supporting the Head Coach with all aspects of the Men\u2019s Wresting program at the University, with primary responsibility for teaching and training student-athletes in the rules, regulations, equipment needs, skills and techniques of wrestling. The position is a fully in-person, part-time appointment not to exceed 25 hours per week. Position Type: Part-time, 12-months, Exempt Department: Athletics Bachelor\u2019s degree required. Degree requirement may be waived with significant relative practical coaching experience. Qualifications: Minimum of 1-year collegiate coaching experience in wrestling or related sport; strong written and verbal communications skills; proven ability to engage, motivate and direct a team of student athletes of diverse backgrounds and experience levels; detail-oriented; ability to instruct skills associated with wrestling; ability and willingness to work a flexible schedule which includes evenings and weekends; ability to support and promote the Franciscan Felician mission and values of the University. Salary range: $10,000-16,000 To Apply: Send cover letter, resume and 2 professional references electronically the Head Coach or via USPS to Mr. Dale Fava, Head Coach Wrestling Felician University Athletics 1 Felician Way Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 Contact Information Office of Admissions Rutherford Campus One Felician Way Rutherford, NJ 07070-1612 Phone: 201.355.1465 Fax: 201.355.1443 Office of The Registrar Lodi Campus 262 South Main Street Lodi, NJ 07644 Phone: 201.559.6043 Fax: 201.559.6066 Email: registrar@felician.edu Contact Us | Directions & Maps | Campus Emergency Information | Request Information | Students Right to Know and Achievement | Privacy policy | Anti-Discrimination Policy | Accessibility TOP Felician University - One Felician Way, Rutherford,