ll-time faculty, adjunct instructors will provide classroom experiences grounded in \u201cbest practices\u201d for higher education and their respective disciplines. Position Type: Part-time, 1-2 courses per semester during the 2025-2026 academic year (spring), maximum 3 days per week. Online format. Department: School of Nursing, Graduate department Required Education: Doctoral degree in Nursing (DNP or PhD) or Master\u2019s degree in Nursing with current enrollment in a doctoral program Qualifications: Certification in area of specialization in primary care. Current, unencumbered RN and APRN license. Demonstrated expertise in the assigned content area. Experience teaching at the graduate level, preferably in online or hybrid formats. Proficiency with learning management systems (e.g., Brightspace/D2L, Canvas, Blackboard). Willingness and ability to support and promote the Felician Franciscan mission and core values of the University. Salary Range:\u00a0 $750-1,100 per credit hour To Apply: Send cover letter, current curriculum vitae, and the names and contact information for two professional references electronically to Associate Dean or via USPS to: Dr. Diana Casianos, Associate Dean School of Nursing Felician University 262 S. Main Street Lodi, \u00a0\u00a0New Jersey 07644 Start Date: Review of candidate materials will begin immediately for Spring 2026 start. Contact Information Office of Admissions Rutherford Campus One Felician Way Rutherford, NJ 07070-1612 Phone: 201.355.1465 Fax: 201.355.1443 Office of The Registrar Lodi Campus 262 South Main Street Lodi, NJ 07644 Phone: 201.559.6043 Fax: 201.559.6066 Email: registrar@felician.edu Contact Us | Directions & Maps | Campus Emergency Information | Request Information | Students Right to Know and Achievement | Privacy policy | Anti-Discrimination Policy | Accessibility TOP Felician University - One Felician Way, Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 201.559.6000 / 201.355.1465 Close GDPR Cookie Settings Privacy Overview S