lician University Our goal is to provide our students with a quality out of class experience that supports and amplifies the teaching and learning process which is the heart of our University. Students may choose from a wide range of opportunities which are designed to help them develop their leadership abilities and to have an enjoyable collegiate experience with great memories that will never end. Office of Student Affairs Dining Services Student Handbook Technology Services Students with Disabilities Residence Life The Center for Student Development and Engagement Campus Safety Counseling and Wellness Services Title IX Campus Ministry University Library University Bookstore Emergency Telephone Numbers Parents Bus & Shuttle Schedules Athletics GET INFO VISIT APPLY News Events My Felician Alumni Giving About About Felician University The University operates on two campuses in Lodi and Rutherford, New Jersey. The University is one of the institutions of higher learning conducted by the Felician Sisters in the United States. Founded by the Felician Sisters of Lodi, New Jersey, it began as Immaculate Conception Normal School with the first summer session commencing on July 5, 1923. History & Tradition Institutional Research Office of the President Senior Administrative Officers Board of Trustees Members Fast Facts Board of Trustees Members Careers at Felician Facilities and Resources Faculty and Staff Directory On Campus Tours Virtual Tour Directions & Maps Academics Academics at Felician University Felician University has four schools and an institute for you to explore a range of undergraduate, pre-professional, certificate, and graduate programs. Search through the program offerings and find the program that is right for you in the School of Arts and Sciences, School of Business and Information Sciences, Education, Nursing, or the Institute for Information Sciences. School of Arts & Sciences School of Education School of Business and Information Sciences School of Nursing The Felician Advantage Lenke Family Center for Innovation Center for Career & Academic Success Center for Academic Technology Honors Program Office of the Registrar Catalogs Institutional Review Board Summer Programs Academic Events Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid at Felician University Inspiring courses that make you think, dedicated faculty who will push you further than you imagined, and hands-on experiences that will shape your career and future. No SAT/ACT Required Affordability Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Adult Undergraduate Admissions Transfer Admissions Our Admissions Representatives High School Guidance Counselor Portal Accepted Students International Students Veterans Services Student Financial Services Make Application Payment Parents Virtual and On Campus Tours Become a Corporate Partner Virtual Appointments Admission Events Campus Life Campus Life at Felician University Our goal is to provide our students with a quality out of class experience that supports and amplifies the teaching and learning process which is the heart of our University. Students may choose from a wide range of opportunities which are designed to help them develop their leadership abilities and to have an enjoyable collegiate experience with great memories that will never end. Office of Student Affairs Dining Services Student Handbook Technology Services Students with Disabilities Residence Life The Center for Student Development and Engagement Campus Safety Counseling and Wellness Services Title IX Campus Ministry University Library University Bookstore Emergency Telephone Numbers Parents Bus & Shuttle Schedules Athletics GET INFO VISIT APPLY Home \\ About Felician University \\ Careers at Felician Security Officers Felician University is presently seeking dedicated and observant Campus Security officers to help protect our campus community, facilities and assets.\u00a0 The Security Officer engages in a wide variety of activities, including but not limited to: conducting active patrols of campus grounds, buildings, parking areas and walkways to ensure safety and security; monitoring surveillance systems and responding promptly to alarms or suspicious activity; enforcing campus policies, rules and regulations in a fair and respectful manner; providing assistance during emergencies, including medical incidents, evacuations, and severe weather events; preparing accurate incident and activity reports; offering directions, information and assistance to students, staff and visitors. Felician University is committed to maintaining a learning and employment environment based upon our core values of Respect for Human Dignity , Compassion , Transformation , Justice and Peace, and Solidarity with People in Need. We offer a \u00a0choice of medical, dental, vision, and life insurance benefits, as well as a retirement plan (403B), tuition remission, and generous time off benefits for full-time employees, and sick time benefits for part-time employees. P osition Type: A variety part-time and full-time shifts available, weekdays, nights and weekends Department: Campus Safety and Security Date Posted: December 19, 2025 Required Education: High school diploma or equivalent required, Associate\u2019s or Bachelor\u2019s degree in Criminal justice or related field a plus Essential Qualifications: Ability and willingness to act to ensure the safety and security of the property, students, staff, faculty and visitors to the University in accordance with University policy, prior security experience in a college/university setting preferred;\u00a0 strong communication and interpersonal skills; ability to remain calm and make sound decisions under pressure; current Security Officer Registration Act (SORA) certification or willingness and ability to attain such upon position confirmation prior to beginning employment; ability to fulfill the physical requirements of the position, including heavy lifting\u00a0within manageable and safe parameters (25-50 pounds), ability to stand, walk, stoop, climb, and bend, and \u00a0ability to work outdoors in all seasons as needed; proven ability to work with a diverse population, experience working with teenagers and young adults preferred; certification in First Aid, CPR, and/or AED a plus; willingness and ability to model, support and promote the Felician Franciscan mission and values of the University. To Apply: Send cover letter, resume, and 2 references electronically to the Director or via USPS to: Mr. Heath James Director, Campus Safety and Security 1 Felician Way Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 Salary: $17.50/hour About Felician University CONTACT INFORMATION Felician University One Felician Way Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 Phone: 201.559.6000 Phone: 201.355.1465 Contact Us | Directions & Maps | Campus Emergency Information | Request Information | Students Right to Know and Achievement | Privacy policy | Anti-Discrimination Policy | Accessibility TOP Felician University - One Felician Way, Rutherford, New Jersey 07070 201.559.6000 / 201.355.1465 Close GDPR Cookie Settings Privacy Overview Strictly Necessary Cookies Powered by GDPR Cookie Compliance (opens in a new tab) Privacy Overview This website uses cookies so that we can provide you with the best user experience possible. Cookie information is stored in your browser and performs functions such as recognising you when you return to our website and helping our team to understand which sections of the website you find most interesting and useful. Strictly Necessary Cookies Strictly Necessary Cookie should be enabled at all times so that we can save your preferences for cookie settings. Enabled Disabled Enable All Save Settings Notifications"}, "https://felician.edu/about-felician-university/careers-at-felician/adjeng/": {"error": "RuntimeError: posting removed (page not found)"}, "https://felician.edu/about-felician-university/careers-at-felician/adjrelst/": {"error": "RuntimeError: posting removed (page not fo